vel: low\n+    follow_ups: >\n+      Decide between a goal that reads the settings without a lifecycle phase, which may need a plugin resolved\n+      offline that the local repository does not hold, and writing the story as \"the plugins bound to validate\n+      run, network closed\"; a test on a fake Maven whose validate phase fails.\n+    status: open\n+  - bug_id: BUG-2026-09-30T221200\n+    date: \"2026-09-30\"\n+    title: \"The option to adopt a Maven plugin does not depend on its edit applying to the POM\"\n+    severity: low\n+    priority: p3\n+    scope: application\n+    what_happened: >\n+      In `designVerification` (`src/application/phases/verification-design.ts`), `adoptable.files` keeps a\n+      recommendation only when its edit applies to the copy, while `adoptable.installs` keeps every installable\n+      recommendation. A Maven recommendation whose edit no longer applied would still offer the resolution, with\n+      an empty list of files. The scenario \"La déclaration s'insère dans le POM octet pour octet, hors le texte\n+      inséré\" says the adoption is not offered then.\n+    what_expected: >\n+      The adoption of a Maven plugin is not offered when the text to replace is no longer present exactly once in\n+      `pom.xml`.\n+    steps_to_reproduce:\n+      - \"Not reachable today: the edit is computed from, and checked against, the same pom.xml of the same copy.\"\n+    root_cause: >\n+      The two lists are computed by separate conditions, and only one of them reads the edit. Introduced by the\n+      branch e12s09. The scenario holds by the construction of `jacocoEdit`, which gives an edit and an install\n+      together or neither; no catalogue target builds an edit that does not apply.\n+    evidence: >\n+      Mutations of the reviewers on 2026-09-30: removing the check `editedFile(...) !== null` from\n+      `adoptable.files` leaves every test green; no test builds an edit that does not apply.\n+    risk_level: low\n+    follow